        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacques-Yves Cousteau, Louis Malle, Peter Joseph\n- Products: The Silent World, Zeitgeist film series\n- Events: 1956 Cannes Film Festival\n- Concepts: documentary films, conspiracy theories, social and economic changes\n\nFacts:\n- In 1956, The Silent World was released as a French documentary film.\n- In 1956, The Silent World was co-directed by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- In 1956, the Palme d'Or at the 1956 Cannes Film Festival went to The Silent World by Jacques-Yves Cousteau and Louis Malle.\n- Between 2007 and 2011, the Zeitgeist film series released three documentary films.\n- The Zeitgeist film series presents a number of conspiracy theories and proposals for broad social and economic changes.\n- Peter Joseph is best known for the Zeitgeist film series.\n- Peter Joseph wrote, directed, narrated, scored, and produced the Zeitgeist film series.",
